#
# THE RELIABLE TEST IS THE SITEMAP, NOT THE REDIRECT. A deleted page leaves the sitemap; an
# undeleted one stays in it and 301s. Measured 2026-09-15: 89 sitemap URLs, and this is the
# ONLY one that redirects. A sitemap that lists a 301'd URL is a mixed signal to Google —
# that is the live cost of leaving the file in place, not a broken redirect.
